+- `createServer` gives its configured session store to the WebSocket message handler, so list requests use the same store as connection and resume handling ([validated by: passes the configured session store to the message handler](../../src/transport/createServerSessionStore.test.ts#L14)).
+- A client sends `{type: 'list_sessions', limit?, before?}` and receives `{type: 'session_list', sessions}` for the socket's authenticated user, with `createdAt` and `updatedAt` serialised as ISO-8601 strings and any client-supplied `userId` ignored ([validated by: lists the authenticated user sessions with pagination and wire-format dates](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L874), [validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L103)).
+- A store without `listFor` answers `{type: 'session_list', sessions: []}`, and a throwing `listFor` logs an error on the `ws` category and answers `{type: 'error', code: 'SERVER_ERROR'}` ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L144)).
+- The validator accepts a bare `list_sessions` frame ([validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame](../../src/transport/ws/listSessionsValidation.test.ts#L4)).
+- Its optional non-negative integer `limit` and optional `before` cursor require a 1–128 character `sessionId` and an `updatedAt` that parses as a valid timestamp; any other payload is rejected with `INVALID_MESSAGE` without calling `listFor` ([validated by: validates and preserves the optional limit and before cursor](../../src/transport/ws/listSessionsValidation.test.ts#L8), [validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L173)).
